sheeettin@gmail.com wrote:
>Well, I don't know about that last part, but everything else works for
>me. They put on some amulets, quaff some potions, and read some
>scrolls--why ahoulsn't they be allowed to read all scrolls, quaff all
>potions, etc?

Game balance.  The game is structured around a lone hero (the player),
and possibly a handful of allies (his pets), battling and defeating a
horde (the monsters).  If the monsters could use all consumable items
that were useful to them, the game would be vastly harder - both because
they would deny the player the use of those consumables, and because the
monsters would themselves benefit from those consumables.

Yes, I know I often criticise Nethack for rather lacking in difficulty
in certain stages of the game, but this is not the way to fix that.
